{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551603-why-shouldn-t-you-blood-bind-dominate-revised-v20","id":1551603,"title":"Why Shouldn't you Blood Bind / Dominate? [Revised / V20]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-06-11T18:14:17-07:00","id":1551603,"title":"Why Shouldn't you Blood Bind / Dominate? [Revised / V20]","content":"Been running VtM for a few years now, and something that got asked a lot was questions like, &quot;Why shouldn't I just try and blood bind the Prince?&quot; or &quot;I could Dominate the Sheriff...&quot; Essentially using blood bonds, Dominate, and Presence to put every major player under your control. And outside of the <i>Vampire Storytellers Handbook Revised </i>explaining that Kindred find such a practice as lazy, there's not a lot of rational to explain why such practices are bad ideas. Or more specifically, it's not very well explained why these will fail.<br /> <br /> Yes, getting caught trying to Blood Bind the Prince, obviously is going to end very very bad for you if caught. But Presence is extremely subtle and can work on lower generation Kindred. Blood Binding, after three drinks, is near permanent. And Dominate has the capability to rewrite memories. I guess I'm just curious why more younger Kindred don't try these tactics, and what tools and reasons do the Kindred in Elysium have to prevent being victims to magical manipulation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28584-matter911","name":"Matter911","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-11T18:19:44-07:00","id":1551604,"title":"","content":"Most younger Kindred don\u2019t have the high levels of Presence and Dominate needed to make these plans work subtly enough to not get caught (and if you do get caught, you\u2019ll probably be the subject of a Blood Hunt). And no elder is going to drink from you three times without very high level Disciplines compelling them to do so (which again rules out younger Kindred).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-11T18:25:35-07:00","id":1551605,"title":"","content":"The Blood Bond is extremely obvious. The Prince stops acting like himself and becomes completely obsessed with some neonate. Other vampires in the city will very quickly figure out what's going on. Maybe they'll kill the neonate, or they'll decide they don't need to obey the Prince, or maybe someone will move to overthrow the Prince, the Anarchs will start acting up. Whatever the case, a Prince who's obviously Blood Bound to a neonate won't retain the respect of other vampires in the city and won't maintain power for long.<br /> <br /> Dominate is fair game. There are likely a number of &quot;puppet Princes&quot; in various domains who are secretly under the control of one (or more) other vampires. The problem with Dominate is that it doesn't work very well (if at all) on vampires who are of lower generation, and it's likely that the Prince will be of lower generation than a neonate.<br /> <br /> Presence can be subtle, or it can be vulgar. As long as a vampire uses Presence subtly they can get away with it. But if a vampire starts tossing it around willy nilly, other vampires won't want to meet with him or her in person. They'll request to work through intermediaries like ghouls or such to pass on messages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-11T18:56:42-07:00","id":1551608,"title":"","content":"I don't think there's any problem with PCs (or NPCs) trying to do any of those things. It's just the potential for failure should be high, and the penalty for failure will result in death, blood hunt, becoming a fugitive, or being subjected to a punishment like them being blood bound themselves to the person they attempted to target. (I'm making a distinction between a tactical use of powers like Dominate and Presence against a vampire versus long term or permanent control over an elder vampire). Elders just won't tolerate this.<br /> <br /> As for Elysium, most STs I know are very clear that ANY use of such powers against another vampire is violation of the rules of Elysium with all the punishment accorded to it.<br /> <br /> However, I think a problem for many STs is that while the NPCs being targeted should be very experienced at detecting such things and being able to avoid them, the STs themselves do not have a mastery of the rules, setting, and game mastering to reflect that. Players will be much more likely to pull one over on the ST than their PCs should be able to do so on certain NPCs. The ST is just too inexperienced to know how to handle the situation. (There's similar problems in other roleplaying games especially when PCs get to the point they can cast powerful magic spells which seldom get used. Many GMs just don't know what to do in response to a &quot;game breaking&quot; event because they don't have much experience with such play, and since there are almost always multiple players and only one GM, the players tend to outthink the GM.)<br /> <br /> A 300 year old elder is going to know someone is attempting to use Presence (even a &quot;subtle&quot; version of it) than a neonate would. Likewise for any successful attempts at Dominate. Why? Because they already would have experienced such things many times when they were younger. They already know the signs that they are being affected, or that someone they know is affected. Mechanically this may just be an excuse for the NPC to spend Willpower every time such things happen. In other situations it may mean that vampire's mentors, friends, or peers notice something is off and quickly figures out why. (Sometimes the ST will need to stack the deck if they think the PCs plans won't work, but if you do this let the players know why you are doing it and the limits you are enforcing OOC. Such times of making things fail automatically need to be restricted and the boundaries known in advance.)<br /> <br /> For the Blood Bond, it may be harder depending on how your play group handles it. I think as written, even the merest hint of some vampire's blood counts as one bond level. In practice, I found this means many stupid attempts by PCs to secretly blood bond others (whether mortals or vampires). In response, I just said that to actually get a true level of the bond, the amount of blood must be noticeable. You just can't blood bond someone without it being obvious.<br /> <br /> Another issue is that ambitious neonates (or whomever) trying to put all major players under their control will almost certainly be caught before they are successful, and they've just made enemies of EVERYONE in the domain. Not just the Kindred they were targeting. Everyone will know that they would lose in such a scenario and thus would want to retaliate against such Kindred as well. The perpetrators will have no friends.<br /> <br /> One option is that such plans will fail because more powerful Kindred have already done this, and neonates won't be successful because they won't be rolling against their targets but the stats of the Kindred really pulling the strings. For example, in the classic Chicago By Night setting, almost all the major players are in fact secretly controlled by either Helena or Menele. The moment one notices this young Kindred doing it (thus stealing their control over this valuable pawn), they are going to be quickly destroyed. Try to blood bond Tyler when she's already bound to Helena? That Kindred never wakes up from their day slumber because Helena's three thousand old ghoul burned down her haven the next day. Try to dominate that vampire who's already dominated by Menele? It fails because Menele's will just overpowers theirs, and the pawn still obeys Menele's much less noticeable power. Not all chronicles should have such powerful methusaleh vampires dictating things, but some level of layering the Jyhad is acceptable and not all vampires active in the city will be known by neonates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-11T22:22:46-07:00","id":1551614,"title":"","content":"Another thing to consider is how likely is that a neonate is going to have any real interaction with the Prince, Primogen, or Senschal when they would be very low on the social heirachy? They would be more likely encountering the Sheriff or Hound then the top players of the fiefdom.<br /> <br /> So unless you have a prestigious sure as a merit, the odds of you having any one on one time with the Prince is unlikely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-11T22:46:00-07:00","id":1551615,"title":"","content":"On an additional mechanical note, a vampire of lower Generation can shrug off Presence just by spending WP; no roll needed. So, like Dominate, it's just note a great tool for just taking over the hearts and minds of the vampires in power on its own.<br /> <br /> Also... what makes anyone think most Elders aren't already under the sway of such things? How many Cam Princes are quietly thralls of Justicars because they're useful but weren't up to snuff to be trusted without such control? Powerful vampires (esp. with some of the Elder Disciplines as shittly designed as those can be) can create far more powerful effects with the same powers by having more time to get big dice-pools/etc. If you're trying to Mesmerize the Prince, you can fail just because someone else already did and got more successes than you.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-11T22:49:31-07:00","id":1551616,"title":"","content":"That's a good point that many Princes could be the pawns of the Camarilla Inner Circle or The True Black Hand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-12T01:01:52-07:00","id":1551619,"title":"","content":"Or &quot;just&quot; a more potent local vampire that prefers not to be in a public position of power. I know I mention the Justiscars, but not everything needs to go the the tippy top of a given Sect's hierarchy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-12T02:28:03-07:00","id":1551620,"title":"","content":"It's not a direct answer but I think this is an area where the VTES card game provides an excellent example of how vampiric influence and control can be represented. Excuse the explanation if you're already familiar with the game.<br /> <br /> In VTES the player can be thought of as representing a methuselah or other very stron behind the scenes power, play consists of recruiting/taking control of vampires by spending 'blood' and then using those vampires to foil the plans of the other players/methuselahs though various means. Vampires that can be recruited include Princes, Justicars, and other high ranks.<br /> <br /> One interesting point is that there are limited opportunities to suborn other players vamps, which I'm assuming is meant to reflect that such opportunites should similarly be limited in the rpg even though the players have more agency.<br /> <br /> As such I think it's a great game for STs to have a go at as it can provide good inspiration for their stories.<br /> <br /> p.s. <a href=\"https://www.vekn.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Home - Vampire: Elder Kindred Network</a> for the VTES card game and all the links and info you need","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11490,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","user":"Dogstar","date":". 06-12-2025, 06:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-12T07:18:05-07:00","id":1551623,"title":"","content":"I will add to what has already been said that a simple Empathy roll is all it takes to take a good guess at someone's intentions, no supernatural powers required. Most humans would not imagine Dominate, Presence or the Blood Bond, but for vampires these are normal facts of life by the time they are allowed to leave their Sire and be somewhat independent. Elders have greater experience, more reason to be suspicious, and a helathy (erm...) tendency to paranoia when it comes to these things.<br /> <br /> Similarly, Subterfuge rolls work to detect schemes, so depending on the circumstances, normal Attribute + Ability rolls can be enough to foil certain attempts, especially against elders with large dice pools which represent their greater experience. <br /> <br /> And I fully second what was said about even elder vampires being involved and pulling the strings, and things potentially failing because they need to be rolled against their bigger dice pools.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-12T10:53:01-07:00","id":1551625,"title":"","content":"So, something I was thinking about a bit more on this:<br /> <br /> In order to put yourself in the position of a younger vampires and why the common sense attitude of &quot;don't try it,&quot; is so effective, it could be useful to think about our natural inclination to accept the &quot;if something's too good to be true...&quot; line of thinking.<br /> <br /> To an extent, the very fact that it seems like it could be so easy to just walk up and mind-control politically important vampires but vampires society isn't just a constant war of blood-bonds, Dominate, and Presence, would naturally ping our social instincts as there being some sort of unseen layer we're not aware of.... even if there wasn't really one. If we're presented with a situation where it seems both, &quot;it's simple and almost anyone could do it,&quot; and, &quot;almost nobody is even thinking about doing it,&quot; are true, our natural inclination is to assume the majority not trying it know something we don't and not trying is the better option (at least in the short term). Learning if they're right or just unwilling to buck a social norm will take time and investigation; likely with a lot of investment into local social structures for people to trust you with information instead of turning you in for obviously plotting to do the &quot;bad&quot; thing nobody thinks should be done.<br /> <br /> Even if all of that uncovers it's just a clever social rouse and you really could mind-whammy your way into local power without any significantly impressive powers of your own, you're then left with a dilemma of what getting that power would accomplish if you undermine the vary social order you're seeking to take the reins of. You, after all, don't want to be the victim of the next vampire that comes along with the same idea, so you need to protect yourself until you're strong enough to not be subjected to the same tactics you used.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-12T14:52:11-07:00","id":1551634,"title":"","content":"Disclaimer only my own perspective, ignore it if you disagree: <br /> Ignoring the logistics; there are tradeoffs to each of these abilities when making pawns.<br /> <br /> The Blood bond makes the character obsessive about you. You blood bonded the Prince. You turned potentially the most powerful person in the city into your stalker. Unlike when you do this to a mortal you are not the one in control of this relationship. <br /> <br /> Dominate strips personality away from the target. How much is up to the st. It's very good for guards. It's less good for major players if you want them to remain as such. You turned a leader into a mindless yes-man. <br /> <br /> Presence is like the blood bond except less predictable. How the target reacts to the emotions you force into him is up to his nature. Kindred are monstrous beasts prone to bouts of berserk frenzy. It's dangerous.<br /> <br /> - Ignoring the tradeoffs and no longer ignoring the logistics.<br /> <br /> It's noticeable. When you do it, and when others see the shift in the targets behaviour to anyone famimiar with the powers.<br /> <br /> These powers are much less effective against Kindred than mortals. <br /> <br /> Kindred punishments include things like hanging your flayed self upside down in Elysium for several weeks. Or months. That's the light sentence. Kindred justice is there to provide a reason not to. The punished will be an example to others.<br /> <br /> These people have security. The guards will shoot you. A lot. Stab you. Stake you. So on. <br /> <br /> These people have supporters, many who will be unknown. They will not like you coopting their ally, pawn, servant, or absolutely worst case their *friend*.<br /> <br /> - so how do you use these powers against other kindred?<br /> <br /> On occasion. When it's sufficently important. As a calculated risk. With a backup plan. And you do it to nudge things, not control them. Pulling off a presence against the prince at the right time, while he's distracted is the thumb on the scale to shift everything.<br /> <br /> Using it as a leash is what you do to kine.<br /> <br /> That's also the final reason. Your kindred are your peers. Don't treat them as cattle. Then they won't have to treat you like a mad dog. A lot of etiquette in all the sects revolve around not having kindred rip each other to pieces. Screwing with that is unwise.<br /> <br /> Not saying it can't or won't happen.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28772-tjale","name":"Tjale","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-12T15:57:29-07:00","id":1551638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tjale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551603-why-shouldn-t-you-blood-bind-dominate-revised-v20?p=1551634#post1551634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Blood bond makes the character obsessive about you. You blood bonded the Prince. You turned potentially the most powerful person in the city into your stalker. Unlike when you do this to a mortal you are not the one in control of this relationship.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a very good point. Blood bond does not mean the target is some lovesick thrall who does your every bidding to win your love. It could mean an abusive lover who physically dominates you to control you until you learn to love her back. Or something else.<br /> <br /> I must admit I often fall into this trap. So many players expect blood bond to mean &quot;I control you&quot;, but that doesn't have to be that way.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-12T16:15:10-07:00","id":1551640,"title":"","content":"For <b>Presence</b> in particular is important to note that anyone can try to resist, anyone at all.<br /> <br /> While that doesn't mean resisting is easy, it does mean that <i>trying</i> isn't something special, and isn't even stated as something you can only do if you know what kind of power it is.<br /> <br /> Dealing with out-of-place emotions isn't completely strange for anyone, and <b>Presence</b> doesn't stop you from noticing that following on your emotions isn't in your best interest.<br /> <br /> All that together points to a harsh truth: <b>Presence</b> <b>is not a subtle power at all</b>. Even &quot;subtle&quot; uses aren't really that subtle, specially considering how overpowering those artificial emotions are.<br /> <br /> If you use <b>Presence</b>, other vampires <b>will know</b>. It isn't an IF, except in quite unique circumstances. Even if your victim doesn't resist, they know just what you did, and they will remember.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-15T19:59:03-07:00","id":1551701,"title":"","content":"In one game my character did have to use Dominate on the prince on one occasion, to snap him out of a mental breakdown at a crucial point. But in terms of having influence in the city I preferred to have him make himself useful and reliable, resulting in his opinion being respected and sought when formulating policy/plans without any supernatural powers being brought into play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-15T23:20:20-07:00","id":1551707,"title":"","content":"There is of course the old GM chestnut of:<br /> &quot;If the players can do it, so can the NPCs.&quot;<br /> <br /> What's stopping the PRINCE from blood bonding or dominating your character? They have the same powers, and substantially more authority to force you into awkward positions. Especially if your neonate seems uppity and plans to take over powerful people in the domain, you can bet the Primogen will react and demand this upstart is controlled or killed.<br /> <br /> Moreover, there are stopgaps.<br /> <br /> Just planning something like this can get you put on the shitlist. Tremere, Malkavians, and Toreadors all have the capacity to read your mind if they so wish, even see glimpses of the future if they're old and powerful enough.<br /> Conspiring with someone else to get your plan working? They stand to gain more by selling you out than by cooperating.<br /> <br /> And even if you succeed, what then? If the Primogen doesn't oust your puppet prince and decapitate you for dessert, someone will be snitching to the higher-ups out of fear or greed, and suddenly you have an Archon hunting for your blood.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla can't have their power players be controlled by younglings. It's bad for business, and it makes the other power players nervous. So they will snuff out any trace of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Furthermore, I believe Carthage should be destroyed.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23835-pang4","name":"pang4","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-16T01:31:10-07:00","id":1551708,"title":"","content":"Blood-bonding someone extremely rich and powerful is a smart play which any vampire can attempt is therefore incredibly tempting for all vampires....which is why all vampires are constantly watching for it to a paranoid degree. <br /> <br /> It is far more likely that a Prince will be mistaken for being blood-bound to a neonate for whom he has a mundane infatuation, than it is that a neonate will secretly blood-bond the prince.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-16T10:08:37-07:00","id":1551723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pang4</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551603-why-shouldn-t-you-blood-bind-dominate-revised-v20?p=1551707#post1551707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is of course the old GM chestnut of:<br /> &quot;If the players can do it, so can the NPCs.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It actually plays in reverse, here: not only do the PCs totally <b>can</b> be Dominated/Presence'd/Bound, if they try to pull off such a stunt, they're more likely to <b>be</b> than to affect an important vampire. Important vampires that can abuse fledglings relatively consequence-free.<br /> <br /> As soon as you make it clear that you can't be trusted as yourself, you won't be yourself for long.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-16T21:03:40-07:00","id":1551732,"title":"","content":"Just to be clear about something: doing this kind of shit to PCs without warning isn't cool, however much sense it makes.<br /> <br /> If players want to try this kind of stunt, it must be clear that a Bond or something is a likely result for failure before they commit to the plan. And PCs having a greater than normal chance of success isn't a bad thing, either, or even receiving uncommon leniency if caught.<br /> <br /> Those considerations are important to make it clear why the setting holds as it does, why NPCs aren't doing such things (and it may even be that someone did and lives as an example for others). For actual uses against PCs, always keep in mind that taking away agency from players is a very delicate thing to do. Characters can suffer, players should have fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-16T23:38:50-07:00","id":1551733,"title":"","content":"I'd like to add that, if one is planning to explore the dynamics of the Bond, Dominate and Presence in the political set up of Kindred society or to give a more realistic feel to it in the games, it can pay off to make some charts of what each power does depending on average dice pools used to roll it. Just because multiple clans have access to these disciplines and all can blood bind others doesn't mean everyone is any good at using them, and it's a tiny fraction of specialised characters who can use them reliably and with consistent effect, enough for plans stretching over centuries.<br /> Let's think about Obfuscate, for example: with Mask of a Thousand Faces, a character with 10 dice has an average of 3 successes when using it. 3 dots in a discipline shows some commitment, and 10 dice means being hyperspecialised for characters from 8th gen downwards. Such hyperspecialised characters still only pull it off regularly up to the changes described for 3 successes. That's a far cry from imagining that appearing with a false appearance is a common feat among vampires, even among the clans with Obfuscate as a clan discipline. And since the roll is Manipulation + Performance, either the character is already an artist and socialite or blackmailer, or he's investing a lot of time in cultivating a social trait and an artistic skill that he mainly uses for this discipline. Most Assamite Warriors, for example, have other traits they are likely to cultivate because they need them more often. Many Nosferatus, too, though it's more sensible for them. Had mastery of this power been common for them, however, their curse would be less relevant in the lore. Setite Priests and Malkavian, on the other side, are more likely to master this power because it's easier to imagine them doing things based on Manipulation and Performance even in their nightly routines, like sacred or inspired art just to give an example.<br /> <br /> I like looking at rules and narrative and lore as a single thing, rather than as competing elements of the game, so this kind of analysis and charting makes sense for me. Your mileage may vary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-17T15:44:04-07:00","id":1551744,"title":"","content":"I will add that most neonates are not going to be all that skilled or subtle in the use of the Disciplines like older ancilliea and elders who are wise to such things and know what to look for.<br /> <br /> They will feel insulted by such heavy handedness or find it amusing and teach neonates a valuable lesson on how to properly use such power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-17T16:26:56-07:00","id":1551746,"title":"","content":"It isn't just being subtle, but being judicious. Even if it were feasible, trying to gain control over society by heavy use of those powers is actually a short and fast route to completely losing control of what's happening. You'll have to micromanage everyone, all the time, that'll quickly overwhelm any manipulator.<br /> <br /> Good uses of those powers demand understanding of people and a lot of effort being put into creating the right circumstances for them. Or rather, most of the time just using them to nudge things a little in an otherwise mundane arrangement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-17T19:52:43-07:00","id":1551747,"title":"","content":"Or to cite Machiavelli: &quot;<u>If you can't be both loved and feared</u>, it is better to be feared than loved.&quot;<br /> <br /> Something people forget in Machiavelli's advice for the leadership class, is that you're supposed to work on cultivating loyalty, trust, and affection towards yourself; even if those are tools you'll use against others rather than offering them sincerely. Ruling purely by force (esp. a style of force that's easily copied) is not the purview of a strong leader that will create an enduring government to rule over. If you can't get people to willingly be on your side by virtue of your skills in promoting the well-being of your city/state/etc., you're destined to quickly become the ruled instead of the ruler (and hopefully your foes don't agree with Machiavelli's advice on what to do with opponents they've defeated).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-09T02:32:06-08:00","id":1557409,"title":"","content":"Takes 3 nights to set up a blood bond. Meaning you need to find a way to trick the prince into drinking your blood three consecutive times. And if they find out, they're probably gonna have you executed.<br /> <br /> Sheriffs are equally as dangerous, because they are supposed to serve as a representative of the prince's authority. Logically speaking, that would mean they have to be sufficiently powerful, or nobody is going to respect them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}